> abiso Z/4 + Z/6, Z/2 + Z/12
Z/4 + Z/6 = Z/2 + Z/12: isomorphic, both Z/2 + Z/12
  phi: (1, 0) -> (1, 9), (0, 1) -> (1, 10)
  psi = phi^-1: (1, 0) -> (2, 3), (0, 1) -> (3, 1)
  check: phi and psi are well defined (relations go to relations), psi phi = 1 and phi psi = 1 on generators
> abiso Z/4 + Z/4, Z/2 + Z/8
Z/4 + Z/4 and Z/2 + Z/8 are not isomorphic
  invariant factors: Z/4 + Z/4 versus Z/2 + Z/8
  how: the invariant factors of a finitely generated abelian group determine it up to isomorphism
> abiso Z/6 + Z/10 + Z/15, Z/30 + Z/30
Z/6 + Z/10 + Z/15 = Z/30 + Z/30: isomorphic, both Z/30 + Z/30
  phi: (1, 0, 0) -> (5, 15), (0, 1, 0) -> (6, 15), (0, 0, 1) -> (0, 16)
  psi = phi^-1: (1, 0) -> (5, 1, 0), (0, 1) -> (0, 5, 1)
  check: phi and psi are well defined (relations go to relations), psi phi = 1 and phi psi = 1 on generators
> abhom Z/4 + Z/6, Z/2 + Z/12
Hom(Z/4 + Z/6, Z/2 + Z/12) = Z/2 + Z/2 + Z/2 + Z/12
  how: the coordinate matrices M with M R_G inside R_H, modulo those with every column in R_H
> abhom Z^2 + Z/3, Z/6
Hom(Z^2 + Z/3, Z/6) = Z/3 + Z/6 + Z/6
  how: the coordinate matrices M with M R_G inside R_H, modulo those with every column in R_H
> abtensor Z/4 + Z, Z/6
(Z/4 + Z) (x) (Z/6) = Z/2 + Z/6
  how: Z^(a b) / (R_G (x) 1, 1 (x) R_H)
> abtor Z/4, Z/6
Tor(Z/4, Z/6) = Z/2
  how: ker(R (x) 1_H) for the free resolution 0 -> Z^b -R-> Z^a -> G -> 0
> abtor Z/12 + Z, Z/8 + Z/3
Tor(Z/12 + Z, Z/8 + Z/3) = Z/12
  how: ker(R (x) 1_H) for the free resolution 0 -> Z^b -R-> Z^a -> G -> 0
> abext Z/4 + Z, Z
Ext(Z/4 + Z, Z) = Z/4
  how: coker Hom(R, H) for the free resolution 0 -> Z^b -R-> Z^a -> G -> 0
> abext Z/12, Z/8
Ext(Z/12, Z/8) = Z/4
  how: coker Hom(R, H) for the free resolution 0 -> Z^b -R-> Z^a -> G -> 0
